From: CIX Neo Build System <noreply@cixtech.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:50:00 +0800
Subject: build: detect the Realtek Kbuild context from src

DKMS supplies KERNELRELEASE to its outer make command and GNU make propagates
command-line variables into recursive invocations. It therefore cannot identify
the inner kernel build. The kernel build system sets src only while reading the
external module Makefile, making it the reliable context test.
---
 rtl-wlan/Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/rtl-wlan/Makefile
+++ b/rtl-wlan/Makefile
@@ -619,3 +619,3 @@
-ifneq ($(KERNELRELEASE),)
+ifneq ($(src),)
 ########### COMMON #################################
 include $(src)/common.mk
